    "topic": "two of Santa's reindeer had different names first",
    "summary": "The 1823 poem 'A Visit from St. Nicholas', first published in the Sentinel of Troy, New York on 23 December 1823 and usually attributed to Clement Clarke Moore, named eight reindeer; the last two were 'Dunder' and 'Blixem', from a Dutch oath meaning 'thunder' and 'lightning'. Moore altered the names several times, to 'Donder' and 'Blitzen' as in his 1844 version; the German spelling 'Donner' became standard from the early 20th century, long after his death.",
